          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For a small, specific leak — a pipe penetration, a gap around a window frame, a hairline crack that only weeps occasionally — Flex Seal works as a temporary patch. For waterproofing a whole basement wall it does not: it is not formulated or tested for sustained hydrostatic pressure across a large area of masonry, and it does not bond to porous block the way a cementitious waterproofer does.",
