            text: "It can hold back a slow weep for a while, but it seals only the surface. Water still travels through the full thickness of the crack, and pressure behind the patch eventually pushes it off — usually at the first heavy rain of the following season. The lasting fix for a leaking crack in poured concrete is a polyurethane injection kit that fills the crack front to back.",
